{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/480713-share-with-me-your-planning-great-sessions-and-campaign-wisdom","id":480713,"title":"Share with Me Your Planning Great Sessions and Campaign Wisdom!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-04-14T14:31:43-07:00","id":480713,"title":"Share with Me Your Planning Great Sessions and Campaign Wisdom!","content":"I'm about to start my Requiem 2e Dark Ages Campaign. Please share with me how you prep great sessions and campaigns!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5685-archivist","name":"Archivist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5685_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-14T16:12:37-07:00","id":480841,"title":"","content":"I don't know about <i>great</i>, but this is how I plan sessions, adventures and campaigns/chronicles.<br /> <br /> Pick a location, a time period, that kind of thing. Consider what to include and exclude. Do I want to focus entirely on vampires, mortals and ghouls, or could I bring in crossovers with other supernatural types? If so, are they as in their gamelines, or something else? What themes do I plan to focus, what kind of power level am I looking at? All of this could be decided with contributions from players who will be in the game, but if I'm pitching to a games society with no guaranteed players I have to decide a lot of this myself.<br /> <br /> Buy a small notebook that can fit in the side pocket of my bookbag. I have a tablet, but actually writing ideas down and flicking from page to page can be helpful, and having it all in one place can be really handy. A page for each clan, a page for each covenant. Not much detail here, just names of NPCs and their roles and cross-references. I also give a page to other supernatural types who might show up, to jot down general ideas, a page to antagonist groups who I plan to have show up, a page or two to specific groups like the Primogen of the city, and a couple pages to prominent mortals.<br /> <br /> I generally aim to have a mix of &quot;adventure&quot; sessions and &quot;night-to-night&quot; sessions, with some overlap. The PCs and NPCs can advance ongoing plans, hunt for blood, and investigate long-term plots, but I will also bring in (apparently) self-contained adventures that cover a session or so. I'll scribble down some adventure hooks. Just a line or two for each right now, some of them ideas like &quot;the ghosts in the old keep become more dangerous on the anniversary of their death&quot; and some questions to be answered later like &quot;why is the Cardinal still in torpor after more than a century?&quot;<br /> <br /> Research! Look through what gaming books and other sources there are for the setting. In my previous <b>Requiem</b> second game I used the Mission from the corebook and related references in previous sourcebooks, and also bought a Lonely Planet guidebook for San Francisco so I'd have a map, street names, landmarks that could be Elysium locations and the like.<br /> <br /> Prepare for things you can't improvise well. For example, I tend to get stuck on wanting NPCs to have interesting and memorable names, so I'll go to somewhere like <a href=\"http://www.behindthename.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Behind The Name</a> or pick up an appropriate sourcebook, name all the NPCs I expect to be prominent, and note down some extra names so when I have to bring in an NPC without warning she won't end up being called &quot;... something German-sounding&quot;.<br /> <br /> I'll look for visuals as well. In my current <b>V20</b> game I have a stack of photos culled from the internet to represent recurring NPCs. After twenty sessions it's getting pretty thick, but it really helps to keep track of who's who, especially in a scene crowded with NPCs. I'll also look for imagery for locations, specific scenes and the like.<br /> <br /> And I'll keep making notes session by session (too many to fit in the small notebook, actually) about what the PCs do and plan to do, what they've discovered, NPCs' ongoing plots and schemes, notes about NPCs I added when they went somewhere I wasn't expecting, and so on.<br /> <br /> Session to session, I'll look over my notes, think about the PCs' and NPCs' plans, see which adventure hooks I haven't brought in yet. I'll prepare an &quot;adventure&quot; more than a &quot;night-to-night&quot; session.<br /> <br /> Good luck!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Craig Oxbrow<br /> <b>The Trinity Continuum</b> freelancer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/221-craig-oxbrow","name":"Craig Oxbrow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar221_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-19T00:02:43-07:00","id":485192,"title":"","content":"So, I'm going to focus on a couple of specific things. If there is something else in particular you want advice one, please feel free to ask more questions.<br /> <br /> <u>Campaign Prep </u><br /> <br /> When I am planning out a campaign, I first come up with at least one 'main plotline'. Something that is big, 'city shaking', and going to happen regardless of who the players are. If I'm feeling ambitious/creative, I come up with three of these 'player neutral' plotlines. That way, you can have the plots push and pull at each other and players have more to figure out. This particular elder is sending out their ghouls looking for something. Is it the blood tome wanted by the Circle of the Crone, or is it the kidnapped Touchstone of one of the Primogen? During my last chronicle, the three plotlines were 1) the mayor was a hunter, and was using his influence to help support hunters in the police, 2) the Seneshal was trying to politically undercut the Prince and take his place, and 3) the Stryx were arriving to wreak havoc, a nefarious menace just there to make things happen in the city. <br /> <br /> The next thing I do is I come up with one plotline for each character. Something personal to their backstory or interests. For example, I had a Mekhet in the Ordo Dracul who was using science to study the vampire condition. The game was set in the 80's. So, her plotline was to investigate the AIDS epidemic, and to find out why vampires who got AIDS suddenly became vulnerable to disease just like a human.<br /> <br /> Between the over-arc plots and the character plots, you should have years of material and the city will seem really hopping.<br /> <br /> <u>Session Prep</u><br /> <br /> Basically, for any individual session, I do the campaign prep in miniature. I pick one major event from my overarching plots. I come up with one scene I can throw at each player for if things get slow for that person. Then, I go to the session and improv the heck out of that. I find that if I show up with more than the core ideas in mind, I start doing things like forcing NPCs to act out of their character and I lose flexibility and adaptability to player surprises. Players never do what you plan. Never. So, I just don't plan on them doing anything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1744-thantrax","name":"Thantrax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1744_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-19T02:24:44-07:00","id":485230,"title":"","content":"There was a short <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/416053-how-do-you-prep-for-a-session\">How do you prep for a session thread</a> in cWoD VtM forum and it's general content may be of some help/use to you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}